# Service Architecture (Layered / Hexagonal)

Inside each backend service, enforce this structure:

- presentation/: controllers, route DTOs, swagger decorators, guards wiring
- application/: use-cases (commands/queries), services orchestration, ports/interfaces
- domain/: entities, value objects, domain services, invariants, domain errors
- infrastructure/: prisma repositories, kafka producer, redis client, config, adapters
- shared/: common utilities (logger, correlation id, errors mapping)

Rules:

- Controllers MUST be thin: no direct Prisma access.
- Infrastructure must implement interfaces defined in application/domain.
- Domain must not import from NestJS, Prisma, or external frameworks.
- CQRS separation:
  - Commands mutate state (write model).
  - Queries do not mutate state.

If any shortcut is taken due to time, document it in the service README under "Trade-offs".
